  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Acting as head chef for the morning, Senya inspects Timur's fish delivery. Noticing the fish looks far from fresh, Senya haggles for a huge discount, shares a cash bonus with the cooks to win their votes, and orders the fish cooked for a Japanese delegation.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Сегодня я сам принимаю рыбу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "У неё какой-то замученный вид.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "timur",
      "t": "Покатайся полдня в грузовике, устанешь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Фёдор, я разберусь без вас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "timur",
      "t": "Да она совсем свежая, точно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "timur",
      "t": "Ещё хорошую скидку тебе сделаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "timur",
      "t": "Ладно, но бери два ящика.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "timur",
      "t": "Слушай, молодец, умеешь хорошо торговаться.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Куда ты столько рыбы набрал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "К нам заехала японская делегация.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Михаил Джекович требует приготовить рыбу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А завтра ещё рыбы закупим.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Сегодня я сам принимаю рыбу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Today I am accepting the fish myself.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'tonight' and finishing on 'fish'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "У неё какой-то замученный вид.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It has a rather exhausted look.' Russian expresses 'having' with the preposition 'by' plus the genitive pronoun and 'view'. Timur answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "timur",
      "t": "Покатайся полдня в грузовике, устанешь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Ride half a day in a truck, you will get tired.' Timur brings out the contrast between 'go for a ride' and 'half a day' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Фёдор, я разберусь без вас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Fyodor, I will sort this out without you.' Notice the reflexive suffix on the verb meaning 'I will sort it out', turning the action back on the subject.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "timur",
      "t": "Да она совсем свежая, точно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Why, it is completely fresh, for sure.' Timur anchors the line on 'yes', while 'exactly' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "timur",
      "t": "Ещё хорошую скидку тебе сделаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will also give you a good discount.' Timur anchors the line on 'else', while 'will do' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "timur",
      "t": "Ладно, но бери два ящика.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Fine, but take two crates.' The meaning hinges on 'all right' working together with 'box' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "timur",
      "t": "Слушай, молодец, умеешь хорошо торговаться.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Listen, well done, you know how to bargain well.' Notice how Russian expresses 'listen' and 'to bargain' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Fedya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Куда ты столько рыбы набрал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Why did you take so much fish?' Fedya anchors the line on 'where to', while 'gathered' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "К нам заехала японская делегация.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'A Japanese delegation has checked in with us.' The meaning hinges on 'us' working together with 'delegation' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Михаил Джекович требует приготовить рыбу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Mikhail Jekovich demands that we prepare fish.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'Mikhail' before landing on 'fish'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А завтра ещё рыбы закупим.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And tomorrow we will buy even more fish.' Senya brings out the contrast between 'and' and 'tomorrow' in a few short words. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
